{title: The King of Love My Shepherd Is}
{artist: Henry W. Baker / St. Columba (Irish)}
{genre: Hymn, Psalm}
{style: Traditional}
{flow: Meditative}
{key: D}
{key_original: Eb}
{tempo: 100}
{time: 3/4}
{c: Chords checked against the four-part harmony of the Cyber Hymnal score (Hymns Ancient and Modern, standard edition (Norwich, England: Canterbury Press, 1994), # 13)}

{start_of_verse: Verse 1}
[D]The King of [A]love [Bm]my [D]Shep[A]herd [D]is,
[D]Whose good[G]ness [D]fail[G]eth [D]never,
[D]I [Bm]nothing [D]lack [Em]if [D]I [A]am [Bm]His
[Bm]And [D]He [G]is [D]mine__[A7]__ for[D]ever.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 3}
[D]Perverse and [A]fool[Bm]ish [D]oft [A]I [D]strayed,
[D]But yet [G]in [D]love [G]He [D]sought me,
[D]And [Bm]on His [D]shoul[Em]der [D]gent[A]ly [Bm]laid,
[Bm]And [D]home, [G]re[D]joic__[A7]__ing, [D]brought me.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 5}
[D]Thou spread’st a [A]ta[Bm]ble [D]in [A]my [D]sight;
[D]Thy unc[G]tion [D]grace [G]be[D]stoweth;
[D]And [Bm]O what [D]trans[Em]port [D]of [A]de[Bm]light
[Bm]From [D]Thy [G]pure [D]cha__[A7]__lice [D]floweth!
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 6}
[D]And so through [A]all [Bm]the [D]length [A]of [D]days
[D]Thy good[G]ness [D]fail[G]eth [D]never;
[D]Good [Bm]Shepherd, [D]may [Em]I [D]sing [A]Thy [Bm]praise
[Bm]Wit[D]hin [G]Thy [D]house__[A7]__ for[D]ever.
{end_of_verse}
